# Pre-commit checks

Before committing any changes, verify the workspace is clean and CI-ready.

## Required steps

1. Run Biome on all modified files: `biome check --write`.
2. Verify the build passes (`tsc --noEmit` or `yarn build`).
3. Never commit files that have unresolved diagnostics or type errors.

## Scope

This applies to every commit — feature work, refactors, docs, config changes. No exceptions.
If a `biome.json` exists in the project, respect it. Do not force-format paths excluded by Biome config.
